Fix silent loss of omitted scenes in FDX. Parse <OmittedScene> into a first-class, reversible representation (per docs/RFC-DRAFT-PRODUCTION.md §7.3 the body stays in the script model and the omission is a record over a contiguous element span starting at a scene heading); the editor model must expose that these elements are omitted; FDX export writes the <OmittedScene> wrapper back with the original paragraph ids and TagNumbers preserved. Unknown nested structure follows the existing embedded-blocks rule. Export of a parsed file keeps the omission; import→export→import is stable. Rendering of omitted scenes in the editor is a later surface stage — out of scope here.